# Library typing (ObjectId / S3 / googleapis)

Full guide: `docs/typescript-library-typing-pitfalls.md`.

## Mongoose ObjectId

- Validate with `mongoose.isValidObjectId(id)`, never `Types.ObjectId.isValid` in new code.
- Construct/parse hex ids through `toObjectId` / `isObjectIdString` in `src/utils/objectId.ts`, not scattered `createFromHexString` / raw `new mongoose.Types.ObjectId(id)` copies.
- If CI reports `Expected 0 arguments, but got 1` or missing `createFromHexString`/`isValid` on `typeof ObjectId`, fix via the helper (`mongoose.mongo.ObjectId` inside `toObjectId`) — do not `@ts-ignore` call sites, and do not use a named `import { ObjectId } from "mongodb"` in serverless route helpers (Vercel has emitted `mongodb_1 is not defined` at runtime).
- `Schema.Types.ObjectId` is for schemas only, not value construction.

## AWS S3

- Call `S3Client.send(new XxxCommand(...))` on the real client.
- Do not invent narrow `send` overload facades and cast `S3Client` into them.
- `Body` exists on get/read outputs (`GetObjectCommandOutput`), not on `PutObjectCommandOutput`.

## googleapis

- When `google.drive` / `google.sheets` reject `auth` on `Options` or methods return `void` instead of `{ data }`, use the existing cast pattern from `src/services/googleSheets/auth.ts`: `as unknown as drive_v3.Options` / `sheets_v4.Options`, with a short comment.
- Fix client factory typing before asserting away missing `.data`.

## Escape hatches

- No `any` / `@ts-ignore` / unexplained double-casts. SDK-boundary casts need a one-line comment naming the library gap.
